[[2047,31,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The windscreen wiper control on the steering column switch unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              selects the\nvarious operating modes of the windscreen wash/wipe.</p><p>The stalk unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              is supplied at\npin 3 of connector D from the ignition-operated line (INT/A) of\nthe relay  \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>R1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               protected by the fuse F14: both are contained\nin the junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Depending on the pre-selected function, the stalk unit H5 (connector A) sends the following control signals to the internal electronic device to the windscreen wiper motor N15:</p><ul><li>from pin 2 for continuous fast operation: the signal reaches\nthe motor directly;</li><li>from pins 3, 4 for continuous slow and medium-fast oeration:\nthe signal arrives from the intermittent device and is then sent\nto the motor</li><li>from pin 5 for intermittent operation: the signal reaches\n the intermittent device and is then sent to the motor; this signal\ndiffers according to adjustment ring position, which adds no resistance,\none resistance or two resistances to the line to obain the three\ndifferent intermittence speeds.</li></ul><p>The windscreen wiper motor  \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is\nthen connected to earth. It consists of the actual geared motor,\nthe end of travel contacts and the electronic adjustment and control\ndevice.</p><p>When operated, the windscreen washer switch\non the steering column switch unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends two signals from\npin 8 and pin 9 of connector A, which reach the pump for operating\nthe windscreen washer \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               directly.</p><p>One of the two signals (pin 6 of connector\nA of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ) is also sent to the electronic device inside the\nwindscreen wiper motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N15</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which manages the operation of\nthe windscreen wiper coupled with the windscreen washer. The same signal\nis also sent as a go ahead to allow the operation of the headlamp washers\n(\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <a href=\"#/3233988\">E3022</a>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p>"]]